<title>USA: U.S. Q3 non-farm productivity rev to -0.3 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. Q3 non-farm productivity rev to -0.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Labor Dept revised estimates of Q3 1996 U.S. productivity/costs, seasonally adjusted annual percent changes from prior quarters, on chain weights basis:</p>
<p>    -	     - Productivity -	  - - -Output- - -</p>
<p>    -	     Q3-R   Q3-P  Q2-R	 Q3-R   Q3-P   Q2</p>
<p> NonFarm	  -0.3   0.2   0.6	   1.8   2.3   4.8</p>
<p> Manufacturing   6.3   6.3   2.9	   5.6   5.4   7.1</p>
<p> Durable Goods   8.3   8.2   3.7	   7.7   7.5  10.7</p>
<p> NonDurables     3.9   3.7   2.0	   3.0   2.7   2.4</p>
<p> Total Business UNCH   0.3   1.2	   2.1   2.4   5.0</p>
<p>    -	     - - -Hours- - -	Hourly Compensation</p>
<p>    -	     Q3-R   Q3-P  Q2-R	 Q3-R   Q3-P  Q2-R</p>
<p> NonFarm	   2.1   2.1   4.1	   3.4   3.9   3.9</p>
<p> Manufacturing  -0.7  -0.8   4.1	   4.6   4.6   5.8</p>
<p> Durable Goods  -0.6  -0.7   6.8	   4.6   4.6   6.8</p>
<p> NonDurables    -0.9  -1.0   0.3	   4.7   4.7   3.7</p>
<p> Total Business  2.0   2.0   3.8	   3.8   4.3   4.3</p>
<p>P-Preliminary. R-Revised.</p>
<p>    -	 Real Hourly Compensation    Unit Labor Costs</p>
<p>    -	     Q3-R   Q3-P  Q2-R	 Q3-R   Q3-P  Q2-R</p>
<p> NonFarm	   1.1   1.6   0.1	   3.7   3.7   3.3</p>
<p> Manufacturing   2.3   2.2   1.9	  -1.6  -1.6   2.8</p>
<p> Durable Goods   2.3   2.2   2.8	  -3.4  -3.3   3.0</p>
<p> NonDurables     2.3   2.3  -0.2	   0.7   0.9   1.6</p>
<p> Total Business  1.5   2.0   0.4	   3.8   4.0   3.1</p>
<p>P-Preliminary. R-Revised.</p>
<p>Wall Street economists had forecast third quarter non-farm productivity to be revised to down 0.1 percent.</p>
<p>Compared to the third quarter of 1995, non-farm productivity rose 0.3 percent in the third quarter, output rose 2.4 percent, hours increased 2.1 percent, hourly compensation was up 3.7 percent, real compensation increased 0.7 percent and unit labor costs rose 3.4 percent, the department said.</p>
</text>
